<title>MOROCCO: Morocco's money supply up to $21.7 bln in March.</title>
<headline>Morocco's money supply up to $21.7 bln in March.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco's Bank al-Maghrib (central bank) released on Wednesday its latest statistics showing that money supply rose to 201.8 billion dirhams ($21.7 bln) in March against 186 billion dirhams in March 1996.</p>
<p>These are figures of Morocco's money supply in billions of dirhams at end period:</p>
<p>    1997	     M1	   M2	    M3</p>
<p>    March	   46.194     99.068     56.554</p>
<p>1996</p>
<p>    March	   43.167     92.294     50.542</p>
<p>1997</p>
<p>    Feb	     46.739     97.719     56.269</p>
<p>1996</p>
<p>    Feb	     43.441     92.295     50.453</p>
<p>The bank defined the agregates as follows:</p>
<p>M1 -- Currency in circulation + Banks cash holdings.</p>
<p>M2 -- M1 + Money + Deposit accounts.</p>
<p>M3 -- M2 + Quasi-money.</p>
<p>($1= 9.3 dirhams)</p>
</text>
